course: dictionary
lesson: 646
title: Bacterial: caused by tiny living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bacterial is an adjective. It tells you that something is caused by bacteria, or has to do with bacteria. Bacteria are tiny living things, far too small to see with your eyes. In «a bacterial chest infection», bacterial tells you which kind of infection it is.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. «Cold, flu, a viral sore throat and a bacterial chest infection look alike, but only one of them is helped by antibiotics.» The words viral and bacterial are set side by side as two different kinds of cause. Ask: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning: caused by bacteria makes sense in the sentence.
explain: The clues also tell you what matters. The sentence says only one of these infections is helped by antibiotics. Because the infection is bacterial, antibiotics can help it. When you read science, look for the words that explain why something happens.
fact: Bacterial means caused by bacteria, or to do with bacteria.
fact: Bacteria are tiny living things, too small to see without a microscope.
fact: Some bacterial infections can be treated with antibiotics; viral infections cannot.
fact: Phrases you may meet are bacterial infection, bacterial growth and bacterial cells.
fact: Not all bacteria cause illness: many are harmless, and some are useful to people.
exercise: «a bacterial chest infection» What does bacterial mean here? | Caused by a bad dream | Caused by a cold wind | *Caused by bacteria | Caused by a broken bone
exercise: Which kind of infection can antibiotics help? | *A bacterial chest infection | Flu | Cold | A viral sore throat
exercise: Sam says bacterial means belonging to the sea. Why might a doctor ask if an infection is bacterial? | Because bacterial means very loud | *Because antibiotics can help bacterial infections | Because bacterial infections are always made of sea water | Because bacterial infections never need any treatment
test: What are bacteria? | Tiny rocks from space | *Tiny living things too small to see | Loud sounds made by machines | Large animals that live in the sea
test: Which phrase means an illness caused by bacteria? | Curt reply | *Bacterial infection | Luminous light | Ancient castle
exam: Which kind of infection can antibiotics treat? | Flu | A cold | *Bacterial infection | Viral infection
